# Bounds the build context to what the Dockerfile actually COPYs: the binary
# named by the BINARY build arg, and `.output/public`. Everything else here —
# `node_modules/` (~200 packages), `.output/server/`, the test suite — is
# irrelevant to the image.
#
# MEASURED, because the obvious rationale for this file turned out to be wrong
# on the builder we use. The claim "without a .dockerignore, docker uploads
# node_modules and the ~100 MB binaries before the first instruction runs" is
# NOT true under BuildKit, which transfers context lazily, per COPY: building
# this image with and without this file reported `transferring context: 1.09kB`
# and `2B` respectively — no measurable difference.
#
# It is kept anyway, for the cases where that laziness does not apply: a remote
# or non-BuildKit builder (DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0) sends the whole directory, and
# `docker build` still walks the tree to evaluate patterns. Treat it as a
# correctness bound on what CAN enter the image, not as the speed fix it was
# first proposed as.
node_modules/
.output/server/
.output/nitro.json
.nitro/
.next/
dist/
test/
app/
*.md

# TWO ARMS SHARE THIS BUILD CONTEXT, and they need different things from it.
# `Dockerfile` (bun) ships a self-contained binary plus `.output/public`, so
# `.next/` above is dead weight to it. `Dockerfile.node` — the CONTROL arm — is
# the opposite: the standalone server IS `.next/`. Re-included narrowly rather
# than by dropping the `.next/` line, so the bun arm's context stays as small as
# it was. Negations must come AFTER the exclusion; docker applies the last
# matching pattern.
!.next/standalone
!.next/static
*.ts
*.mjs
*.log
bun.lock
tsconfig.json

# NOT excluded: `knext-bun-exec-*` itself. The Dockerfile COPYs whichever one
# `--build-arg BINARY=...` names, and a .dockerignore cannot be parameterised by
# a build arg — so on a tree that has built several arches, every one of them is
# still uploaded. Stated rather than silently accepted; the alternative is a
# per-arch staging dir, which is more machinery than the saving justifies.
*.build-provenance.json
